{"id": "q0360", "pool": "easy-fact", "tier": "balanced", "audio_s": 14.49, "n_chunks": 15, "n_concurrent": 15, "gen_active_at_eot": true, "eot_score": 0.6827, "eot_read_ms": 30, "reference_answer": "Jimi Hendrix", "query": "\"After stints backing Little Richard and the Isley Brothers, who was discovered leading \"\"Jimmy James and the Blue Flames\"\" at the Caf Wha? in New York and taken to London on 26 September 1966 to make hit records?\"", "transcript": "After stints backing Little Richard and the Iley Brothers, he was discovered leading Jimmy James and the Blue Flames at the Cafe Wha? in New York and taken to London on 26 September 1966 to make hit records.", "first_audio_ms": 33, "stall_pcm_s": 2.96, "relay_first_audio_ms": 868, "spoken_s": 6.48, "mode": "escalated", "relay": "The person who discovered leading Jimmy James and the Blue Flames was Jimi Hendrix.", "expert_answer": "Jimi Hendrix.", "expert_latency_s": 2.54, "stall_ms": 33, "relay_ms": 3853}
{"id": "q0365", "pool": "easy-fact", "tier": "balanced", "audio_s": 5.11, "n_chunks": 6, "n_concurrent": 6, "gen_active_at_eot": true, "eot_score": 0.198, "eot_read_ms": 28, "reference_answer": "MARGARITA", "query": "Which cocktail comprises Tequila, Lime or Lemon juice, and Orange-flavoured liqueur?", "transcript": "Which cocktail comprises tequila, lime or lemon juice and orange-flavoured liqueur?", "first_audio_ms": 815, "spoken_s": 7.16, "mode": "local", "answer": "The cocktail that comprises tequila, lime or lemon juice, and orange-flavored liqueur is called a Margarita.", "answer_ms": 4279}
{"id": "q0382", "pool": "easy-fact", "tier": "balanced", "audio_s": 4.91, "n_chunks": 5, "n_concurrent": 5, "gen_active_at_eot": true, "eot_score": 0.2969, "eot_read_ms": 28, "reference_answer": "$85,000", "query": "In the very first Boston Marathon, 15 runners competed. How many finished?", "transcript": "In the very first Boston Marathon, fifteen runners competed. How many finished?", "first_audio_ms": 813, "spoken_s": 10.88, "mode": "local", "answer": "The very first Boston Marathon took place in 1897. Fifteen runners started the race. All fifteen finished!", "answer_ms": 6223}
{"id": "q0388", "pool": "easy-fact", "tier": "balanced", "audio_s": 3.12, "n_chunks": 4, "n_concurrent": 4, "gen_active_at_eot": true, "eot_score": 0.3669, "eot_read_ms": 29, "reference_answer": "The River Taff", "query": "Can you name the river that flows through Cardiff?", "transcript": "Can you name the river that flows through Cardiff?", "first_audio_ms": 839, "spoken_s": 3.88, "mode": "local", "answer": "The river that flows through Cardiff is the Taff.", "answer_ms": 2294}
{"id": "q0395", "pool": "easy-fact", "tier": "balanced", "audio_s": 2.96, "n_chunks": 3, "n_concurrent": 3, "gen_active_at_eot": true, "eot_score": 0.4861, "eot_read_ms": 29, "reference_answer": "Stenographer", "query": "What is the American word for a short-hand typist?", "transcript": "What is the American word for a shorthand typist?", "first_audio_ms": 32, "stall_pcm_s": 2.96, "relay_first_audio_ms": 916, "spoken_s": 4.6, "mode": "escalated", "relay": "The American word for a shorthand typist is stenographer.", "expert_answer": "The American word for a shorthand typist is **stenographer**.", "expert_latency_s": 1.6, "stall_ms": 32, "relay_ms": 2907}
{"id": "q0409", "pool": "easy-chat", "tier": "balanced", "audio_s": 3.01, "n_chunks": 4, "n_concurrent": 4, "gen_active_at_eot": true, "eot_score": 0.1799, "eot_read_ms": 30, "reference_answer": null, "query": "What is the Philly Special and when was it used ?", "transcript": "What is the Philly Special and when was it used?", "first_audio_ms": 826, "spoken_s": 25.16, "mode": "local", "answer": "The Philly Special is a trick play used in American football, most famously during Super Bowl LII. It involves the quarterback taking the snap while in the end zone and throwing a short pass to a teammate who then throws it back to the quarterback for a touchdown. This play was used by the Philadelphia Eagles against the New England Patriots in February 2018.", "answer_ms": 15085}
{"id": "q0421", "pool": "easy-chat", "tier": "balanced", "audio_s": 4.21, "n_chunks": 5, "n_concurrent": 5, "gen_active_at_eot": true, "eot_score": 0.1032, "eot_read_ms": 29, "reference_answer": null, "query": "Explain the best way to swing a golf iron compared to a golf driver.", "transcript": "Explain the best way to swing a golf iron compared to a golf driver.", "first_audio_ms": 797, "spoken_s": 66.56, "mode": "local", "answer": "Golf drivers and irons are both used to hit golf balls, but they serve different purposes on the course. Drivers are designed for hitting long-distance shots from the tee box. They have a larger head and a longer shaft, which helps generate more power and distance when striking the ball. Drivers are typically used on par 3, 4, and 5 holes where you want to cover as much ground as possible with your first shot, especially off the tee or sometimes from fairways in shorter distances. On the other hand, irons are used for more precise shots over shorter distances. They come in various numbers, like 3-iron, 5-iron, etc., with lower numbers generally being easier to hit and having less loft, while higher numbers provide more lift and control, making them useful for approach shots into the green. So, a driver is best for long, powerful drives, while irons offer better control and accuracy for shorter, strategic shots around the course.", "answer_ms": 43058}
{"id": "q0426", "pool": "easy-chat", "tier": "balanced", "audio_s": 2.9, "n_chunks": 3, "n_concurrent": 3, "gen_active_at_eot": true, "eot_score": 0.11, "eot_read_ms": 29, "reference_answer": null, "query": "What is the purpose of a shot clock in basketball?", "transcript": "What is the purpose of a shot clock in basketball?", "first_audio_ms": 816, "spoken_s": 28.16, "mode": "local", "answer": "The purpose of a shot clock in basketball is to keep the game moving and prevent teams from holding the ball for too long. It ensures that there's a rhythm to the game and encourages teams to make quick decisions, whether it's taking a shot or passing the ball. Without a shot clock, games could drag on with one team simply standing around waiting to shoot, which would slow down the pace and make the game less exciting for everyone watching.", "answer_ms": 16826}
{"id": "q0437", "pool": "easy-chat", "tier": "balanced", "audio_s": 2.16, "n_chunks": 3, "n_concurrent": 3, "gen_active_at_eot": true, "eot_score": 0.4869, "eot_read_ms": 29, "reference_answer": null, "query": "What is the GE Dash 8-32BWH", "transcript": "What is the GE-832BH?", "first_audio_ms": 34, "stall_pcm_s": 2.96, "relay_first_audio_ms": 919, "spoken_s": 18.64, "mode": "escalated", "relay": "The **GE-832BH** appears to refer to the **GE Dash 8-32BWH** — a **diesel-electric passenger locomotive** built by **General Electric** for Amtrak in the early 1990s. It is also known as the **P32-8BWH**.", "expert_answer": "The **GE-832BH** appears to refer to the **GE Dash 8-32BWH** — a **diesel-electric passenger locomotive** built by **General Electric** for Amtrak in the early 1990s. It is also known as the **P32-8BWH**.", "expert_latency_s": 9.42, "stall_ms": 34, "relay_ms": 11691}
{"id": "q0452", "pool": "easy-chat", "tier": "balanced", "audio_s": 1.34, "n_chunks": 2, "n_concurrent": 2, "gen_active_at_eot": true, "eot_score": 0.1103, "eot_read_ms": 26, "reference_answer": null, "query": "Who wrote Les Miserable", "transcript": "Who wrote Les Miserables?", "first_audio_ms": 804, "spoken_s": 4.76, "mode": "local", "answer": "\"Les Misérables\" was written by Victor Hugo.", "answer_ms": 2656}
{"id": "q0461", "pool": "easy-chat", "tier": "balanced", "audio_s": 2.0, "n_chunks": 2, "n_concurrent": 2, "gen_active_at_eot": true, "eot_score": 0.0528, "eot_read_ms": 28, "reference_answer": null, "query": "how do you rate strength of tornado", "transcript": "How do you rate strength of tornado?", "first_audio_ms": 811, "spoken_s": 32.24, "mode": "local", "answer": "The strength of a tornado is rated using the Enhanced Fujita Scale, or EF Scale. This scale rates tornadoes from EF0 to EF5 based on the damage they cause. For example, an EF0 has wind speeds around 65 to 85 mph and causes minor damage, while an EF5 can have winds over 200 mph and results in catastrophic destruction. Meteorologists use this rating to assess tornado intensity after it occurs.", "answer_ms": 18448}
{"id": "q0468", "pool": "easy-chat", "tier": "balanced", "audio_s": 1.82, "n_chunks": 2, "n_concurrent": 2, "gen_active_at_eot": true, "eot_score": 0.0672, "eot_read_ms": 29, "reference_answer": null, "query": "What does the Constitution do?", "transcript": "What does the Constitution do?", "first_audio_ms": 778, "spoken_s": 11.24, "mode": "local", "answer": "The Constitution sets up the government, divides power among branches, protects individual rights, and provides procedures for changing the document itself.", "answer_ms": 6060}
